-- A generic function value returned with an inferred return type. GN030 says
-- a generic function type is written only as the type of a parameter, and
-- `let g = identity` is GN015, but `wrap` itself is accepted; each call of it
-- is then GN015 "`T` can't be inferred here: give it explicitly after the name
-- of the function", which names a `T` that `wrap` doesn't have.
-- Expected: one error on `wrap` (GN030: annotate a return type that isn't generic).
function identity = <T>(value: T): T => value
function wrap = () => identity
console.log(wrap()(1), wrap()("a")) -- prints: 1 a
